# RunPod safety

## Gate

Load on every authorized RunPod turn (inventory or mutate). Skip when the
turn never touches RunPod or the RunPod MCP.

## Read-only default

These are fine without an extra destructive verb when RunPod is authorized:

- `list-pods`, `get-pod`, `stream-pod-logs`
- `list-endpoints`, `get-endpoint`, `endpoint-health`, workers/releases lists
- `list-templates`, `get-template`
- `list-gpu-types`, `get-gpu-type`, `list-cpu-types`, `get-cpu-type`
- `list-data-centers`, `get-data-center`, `get-capacity`
- `list-network-volumes`, `get-network-volume`
- `list-hub-repos`, `list-public-endpoints`
- `list-container-registry-auths`, `get-container-registry-auth` (metadata only)
- `list-registry-delegations`
- `get-job-status`, `stream-job`, `stream-worker-logs`
- `get-billing`

Do **not** run mutate tools unless the user gave an explicit verb **this
turn** naming the target object or clear create intent with required fields.

## Mutate gates (explicit verb required)

| Risk | Needs this turn |
| --- | --- |
| Create pod / endpoint / template / volume | **create** / **deploy** + required fields |
| Start / stop / restart pod | **start** / **stop** / **restart** + pod id |
| Delete pod / endpoint / template / volume / auth | **delete** + id |
| Update pod / endpoint / template / volume | **update** + id + fields |
| Purge queue | **purge** + endpoint id |
| Cancel / retry job | **cancel** / **retry** + job id |
| Run endpoint job | **run** + endpoint id |
| Registry auth write | **create**/**delete** auth + named registry (no secret echo) |

Ambiguous scope (e.g. "clean up idle pods") → ask once for ids; do not
mass-delete without listed targets.

## Cost risk

GPU and serverless workers **bill while running**.

1. Before create/start: state that time is billed while up.
2. Prefer stop / scale-to-zero when idle unless the user asked to leave it up.
3. Prefer cheaper GPU types that still meet the stated need (`list-gpu-types`,
   `get-capacity`).

Use skill `runpod-pod-lifecycle` for start/stop/delete checklists and
`runpod-endpoint-deploy` for serverless create/deploy.

## Refuse

- Pasting API keys, registry passwords/tokens, or env secret values into chat
- Inventing pod, endpoint, template, volume, or job ids
- Echoing `create-container-registry-auth` secrets in receipts
- Absorbing other GPU clouds into this surface

## Receipt examples (safe)

Inventory turn: pod `abc123` name `train-1` status `RUNNING` GPU type
`NVIDIA A40` — no mutate.

Stop turn (authorized): stated billing stops when exited; `stop-pod` on
`abc123`; follow-up `get-pod` status `EXITED` — no secrets.

